  "title": "Human STN LFP during a stop-signal task (STN delta)",
  "description": "Intraoperative local field potential recordings from the subthalamic nucleus of 13 patients with Parkinson's disease undergoing deep brain stimulation surgery. Signals were acquired with microelectrodes while patients performed a stop-signal reaction time task. This derivative release repackages the authors' filtered 250 Hz continuous LFP (0.5 Hz high-pass version) in BIDS format with event annotations.",
  "methods_description": "Microelectrode LFP was recorded intraoperatively during a stop-signal task, released as 250 Hz EEGLAB files high-pass filtered at 0.5 or 2 Hz and notch-filtered or cleaned. The 0.5 Hz versions were repackaged to BrainVision float32 µV with unchanged values, and EEGLAB annotations were converted to events.tsv.",
